  "content": {
    "id": "p42-q6",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A member of an indoor cricket team, playing a match in a gymnasium, hits a ball that follows a path given by $y=-0.1x^2+2x+1$, where $y$ is the height above ground, in metres, and $x$ is the horizontal distance travelled by the ball. The ceiling of the gymnasium is 10.6 metres high.\nDetermine whether the ball will intersect with the ceiling.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. Setting $10.6=-0.1x^2+2x+1$ gives $\\Delta=0.16>0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}10.6&=-0.1x^2+2x+1\\\\0.1x^2-2x+9.6&=0\\\\\\Delta&=(-2)^2-4(0.1)(9.6)\\\\\\Delta&=0.16>0\\end{align*}$$\nThere are two real intersections with the ceiling line. Their horizontal distances satisfy $x=\\frac{2\\pm0.4}{0.2}=8$ or $12$ metres. The ball first hits the ceiling after travelling 8 metres horizontally.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
